Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?gvn:=20cross-block=20pure=20CSE=20for=20int?=
 =?UTF-8?q?eger=20Mul=20via=20use-renaming=20=E2=80=94=20sieve's=20triple?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20i*i=20becomes=20one?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The B1 work-order item, root-caused and fixed at the source: dominator-
based GVN restricted pure-expression CSE to SAME-BLOCK only ("Cross-block
CSE creates Copies whose source values may have their registers reused by
the allocator before the Copy executes") — a Copy-form workaround for an
old allocator hazard. sieve's count_primes computed i*i three times per
outer iteration (header test, j-init under the sieve[i] branch, latch
test) where gcc 14.2 keeps ONE multiply; 102 insns in the region vs
gcc's 56.

The fix removes the Copy entirely: a cross-block pure hit now DELETES the
dominated instruction and renames its uses onto the dominator's value
(apply_pending_renames, applied after the DFS walk).  No Copy is
inserted, so the historical stale-home hazard does not exist — the
register allocator sees a plain SSA value with dominated uses.

Scope, arrived at empirically (each widening was measured against the
803-test corpus, SSA-validated, before the next decision):
- INTEGER Mul only.  Add is deliberately excluded: the loop passes
  structurally consume Add shapes (the stencil matcher's documented
   exit-compare form; find_iv_in_loop's latch-local IV-
  increment contract) — a broad Add rename flipped stencil_vectorize's
  checksum and broke 21 unroll/vectorize corpus shapes.  Mul has no such
  structural consumers.  GEP/GlobalAddr stay retained-across-blocks by
  design (gep_value_numbers); Cast keeps the cross-signedness machinery;
  float BinOps are FMA-contraction-shape-sensitive.
- The dominated dest must not feed any Phi incoming (phi_incoming_feeds):
  the unrollers thread exit/IV phis off latch-local bookkeeping, and
  sharing the IV-increment Add with a body value (legal SSA, gcc's own
  form) collapses the latch after cfg_simplify — measured: the
   accumulator returned the IV instead of the sum.
- Multi-def dests keep their instruction (one definition of a redefined
  id cannot be deleted).

Measured: sieve count_primes 3 imull -> 1 (gcc parity), region 102 -> 95
insns, benchmark ratio vs gcc -O2 1.116x -> 1.053x (55.8ms vs 53.0ms
median-of-7, bit-exact output).  The 803-test regression corpus with
CCC_VALIDATE_SSA=1: 774/0 (identical to the pre-change control).  The
204-workload benchmark output oracle: 204/204 bit-exact.  cargo --lib
3347/0 (the cross_block_cse contract test advanced from "must not CSE"
to "must rename", with an Add-exclusion pin in the same function).
ci_local --fast: 64/64 ALL GREEN (the env-hygiene ratchet caught and
rejected a per-call env read in the first draft — the debug print now
reuses the existing CSE trace site).
